quran[16]{c,v,t}:
  7,105,What behooves me is to say (nothing) about Allah but the truth. I have indeed brought you a clear sign from your Lord. So send away with me the Children of Israel (setting them free of your yoke of slavery).’
  7,106,"He (Pharaoh) said: ‘If you have brought a sign, then bring it (to the fore) if you are truthful.’"
  7,107,"So Musa (Moses) put his staff (down), and at once it changed into a veritable serpent."
  7,108,"And he drew out his hand (after putting it into his collar opening), and that (too) at once became (radiant) white to the viewers."
  7,109,The chiefs of Pharaoh’s people said: ‘He is undoubtedly an expert magician.
  7,110,"(O people!) He seeks to drive you out of your land. So, what do you advise?’"
  7,111,"They said: ‘Put (the matter) of Musa (Moses) and his brother off (for a while), and send out heralds to (different) cities to summon (magicians)."
  7,112,They will bring you every skilful sorcerer.’
  7,113,And the magicians came to Pharaoh and said: ‘There should certainly be some reward for us if we overmaster.’
  7,114,"Pharaoh said: ‘Yes, of course; (what to talk of a simple reward! In that case) you will be amongst the privileged ones (of my court).’"
  7,115,(The magicians) said: ‘Musa (Moses)! Either you throw (your object) or we become (the first) to throw.’
  7,116,"Musa (Moses) said: ‘You throw (first).’ So when they threw (their strings and sticks on the ground), they bewitched the eyes of the people, and struck them with awe, and brought (forth) an extremely effective magic."
  7,117,And We revealed to Musa (Moses): ‘(Now) throw your staff (on the ground).’ Then at once it began swallowing up what they had fabricated through deception.
  7,118,"So, the truth was established, and everything that they had been doing was proved false."
  7,119,"So, they (the representatives of Pharaoh) were vanquished on the spot and backed away humiliated."
  7,120,And (all) the sorcerers fell down prostrate.
